.TH DANBY-MANYSPECIES 1
.SH NAME
danby-manyspecies \- one prey population shared by two predator species
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/manyspecies
.SH MODEL
X' = rX(1-X/K)-a1XY-a2XZ;
Y' = c1 a1XY-d1Y;
Z' = c2 a2XZ-d2Z.
.PP
Y and Z exploit the same prey X but may have different attack, conversion,
and death rates.  Their zero-growth prey requirements d1/(c1a1) and
d2/(c2a2) explain competitive exclusion except at a parameter coincidence.
.SH DISPLAY
Three histories and three directly editable state bars show which predator
persists, how quickly exclusion occurs, and how the prey responds.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag a state bar to change an initial population.  The eight tracks set prey
growth and capacity followed by attack, conversion, and death for each
predator.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/manyspecies.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/manyspecies.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/populations.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-foodchain (1),
.IR numerics (2)
